on\/receive(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" returns. Batches that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arrive meanwhile wait in a buffer of the destination’s own, which drops its oldest batch when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"full, so a destination that falls behind loses batches rather than holding up the others.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" should return promptly and honour cancellation: a delivery waits for it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before it completes, and cancels it when the delivery is cancelled. A destination handles its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own errors (a failed upload, say); the delivery has none to receive."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When a tracker keeps its records in a store, returning from "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" is what tells the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store a batch arrived: once every destination has returned for it, uncancelled, the store"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forgets those records. A destination that buffers or retries should return only once the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch is somewhere it won’t be lost; a record whose "},{"code":"EventRecord.isRedelivered","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is set may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have reached it in an earlier run."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"What a destination receives is narrowed by modifiers rather than by code of its own:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for the consent categories it serves, "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":". A destination given none receives every record as tracked."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/accepting(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/droppingCallSite()","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/redactingSensitiveValues()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"Where a delivery sends events: a plain sink that records the batches it receives.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Destinations/documentation/Destinations/Destination/receive(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Records ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"required":true,"url":"\/documentation\/destinations\/destination\/receive(_:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"receive","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"([","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventRecord","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Events11EventRecordV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"]) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination\/receive(_:)","type":"topic","role":"